    "path": "opentelemetry_sdk::logs::concurrent_log_processor::SimpleConcurrentLogProcessor",
    "name": "SimpleConcurrentLogProcessor",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "opentelemetry_sdk",
    "version": "0.31.0",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct SimpleConcurrentLogProcessor<T: LogExporter>",
    "docs": "A concurrent log processor calls exporter's export method on each emit. This\nprocessor does not buffer logs. Note: This invokes exporter's export method\non the current thread without synchronization. i.e multiple export() calls\ncan happen simultaneously from different threads. This is not a problem if\nthe exporter is designed to handle that. As of now, exporters in the\nopentelemetry-rust project (stdout/otlp) are not thread-safe.\nThis is intended to be used when exporting to operating system\ntracing facilities like Windows ETW, Linux TracePoints etc.",
